<title>USA: Finish Line stake cut by Vinik Group.</title>
<headline>Finish Line stake cut by Vinik Group.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1997-04-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>A group led by former Fidelity Magellan Fund manager Jeffrey Vinik on Wednesday said it cut its stake in Finish Line Inc. to 840,100 shares or a 4.96 percent stake from 1,175,100 shares or a 6.9 percent stake.</p>
<p>In a filing with the U.S. Securities and Exchange Commission, the group said it sold shares betweeen April 15 and April 21 at $12.64 to $15.99 each.</p>
<p>Finish Line, based in Indianapolis, retails athletic footwear and clothing.</p>
